# cmd.exe resolves `call :label` and `goto` by scanning the batch file for
# CRLF line endings; in an LF-only file the scan's byte offsets drift, so
# labels early in the file still resolve while later ones fail with
# "The system cannot find the batch label specified". The release zips are
# built on a Linux runner, which would check these out as LF without this
# rule. Force CRLF in the working tree on every platform.
*.bat text eol=crlf
